      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>To receive the air sealing rebate: your home must have at least 3 air changes per hour as determined by the initial energy assessment; you must have 1.5 or fewer air changes per hour post-renovation; and you must install an HRV to ensure balanced ventilation in your home.

The total air sealing rebate is $5,000 per building when the building meets or exceeds the air sealing target.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>To receive the insulation rebate for above-ground walls, you must at least double the existing insulation level. For example, if the original insulation value is R20, you must increase the insulation to R40 or greater.

The total for the insulation rebate is up to a maximum of $26,500 per building up to a maximum of $12,000 for insulating above-ground walls;

The insulation rebate amount for above-ground and below-ground walls is based on the percentage of the total wall area youve insulated. For example, if you insulate 50 per cent of your homes total above-ground walls, youll receive $6,000. If you insulate 100 per cent of your homes total above-ground walls, youll receive $12,000.

You can apply multiple times as you add insulation to your homes above-ground or below-ground walls, up to a maximum of $12,000 for each wall type.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>To receive the Yukon good energy attic insulation rebate the insulation level must be R40 or less prior to the renovation; and
you must increase it to R60 or greater.

You are eligable for us to $2500 for insulating your attic.You must insulate the entire attic. You can apply for the attic insulation rebate only once per building.</ceilings>
                <foundation>To receive the insulation rebate for below-ground walls the insulation level must be R20 or less prior to the renovation; and
you must increase it to at least R20.

The insulation rebate amount for below-ground walls is based on the percentage of the total wall area youve insulated. For example, if you insulate 50 per cent of your homes total below-ground walls, youll receive $6,000. If you insulate 100 per cent of your homes total below-ground walls, youll receive $12,000.</foundation>
                <windows>Replace existing windows with ENERGY STAR® windows and get: a $120 rebate per window; to a maximum rebate of $1,800 per home.</windows>
                <VentilationSystem>The heat-recovery ventilator (HRV) must: be listed with the Home Ventilating Institute; and have a 64% or higher sensible recovery efficiency at -25°celsius.

Rebate amounts are: $750 for HRV; and $750 if youre installing ducting for the HRV. You can get up to a maximum of $1,500 per building.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>You are eligable for up to $8000 when installing a cold climate air source heat pump in your home. For more information please visit YG's website at: https://yukon.ca/en/heating-system-rebate.</HeatingSystem>
                <Renewables>Renewable energy systems that generate electricity from: solar photovoltaic (PV) are eligible for the rebate. All systems must be residential installations.

Grid-tied clients must be part of the micro-generation program. All grid-tied systems must be pre-approved by the Energy Branch.

Rebate amount: Get a rebate of $800 per kilowatt of generating capacity to a maximum of $5,000 per system per year.</Renewables>
            </RURComments>
